Z||000000||danny boy||03-24-2001||12:14 AM|||| I started this new job in November af last year.Every day I drive past this Fiero.The car is Blue with grey ground effects,a luggage rack and tan int. It also has GT on the qtr glass. I'm wondering everday if its an 87 SE that got 85GT qtr glass.The paint looks original. <BR>This has bugged me since the first time I saw it.Well, today the owner was by the car so I stopped. I asked him about it and he said it was the factory paint."oh, so it's an 87." "No,its an 85." he is the second owner of the car and knew the first owner well.He said the car was ordered that way and with those seats,too.Seats?<BR>upon looking inside I saw the oddest looking seats I've ever seen.They were tan pigskin with that wooly mammoth stuff in the middle. they also had the speaker holes.These were not slip on covers they were seats. I asked if it was for sale, but he told me it was sold and the guy was on his way to get it. <BR>oh, well,I don't need another one anyway,even if it was a 50K mile car.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Kelvin Vivian||03-24-2001||12:34 AM||||My guess is that the Fiero is a 1985 GT that has been repainted blue.  There must be a way somehow to figure out what the original paint color was. Might have been white or red.<P>I believe most, if not all, blue Fieros have a grey interior.  I've never seen a blue 1987 SE, and if someone does have one, it would be neat to see a picture of one... I've only seen blue GTs and blue coupes.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402882&Sequence=1&res=high"> <BR>1987 Fiero SE 4-cyl, 5-spd Isuzu, Medium Red Metallic<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44568420&Sequence=1&res=high"> <BR>The 4-cyl Tech-4 Duke tucked away...<P>Kelvin Vivian<BR>87 SE<BR>88 GT||||reg||3
